A||N||2||Giles||more power from fourbanger||||1||
Z||000000||Giles||02-13-2000||01:13 PM||||i have a cylinder head from an 84 fiero parts car i bought a couple months ago, and i want to do a bit of work on it.  I checked it for        and found none.  next, i ported and polished the whole thing and i'm thinking of milling the head for higher compression.  Do you know how much i could mill before ramming the valves into the pistons?  I still want to run pump gas, so i don't want to go too far.  i'm looking for about 10 to 1 right now.  Also, i'm looking for some other inexpensive ways to get more power from this 2.5.  any suggestions would be appreciated.  thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||02-13-2000||02:05 PM||||When I redid our 2.5, put 30 over pistons in it and had the head milled 10 and it seems to have very good power.  Never had it on a dyno,so can't speak to facts and figures,just know it runs really good and has very good pick up.  Did not use a "Fiero head" on the motor.  The head that came off had 4 cracks in it and every other one I dug up was the same.  The book says it won't work, but I got to looking at a head from a 1979 Monza 2.5 fwl car. GM made 109 changes in the 2.5 head  in a 9 year period.  Most of the Fiero heads I have seen use the chamber that has a tapered peak between the valves.  The head I used is an open oval. To make it work, you have to change one soft plug inside the head(1/2" I think) and the  large one on the outside of the head, and grind a little off the thermostat housing(only a hole flange) but it works and does not stand nearly the chance of cracking that the "v" combustion chamber heads do.  All I know is that the engine runs very well and does not lack for power at all!  I would think that a good header would gain you some power.  Let us know if you come up with an easy effective mod that increases your power.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Giles||02-14-2000||05:23 PM||||Thanks a lot, sage.  I'll probably do what you suggested.  Just need to get the  money for the headers now....||||reg||1
